            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral idiopathic trochleitis as a cause of frontal cephalgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>476-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1526-4610.2008.01259.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Trochleitis is defined as the inflammation of the trochlea and peri-trochlear region, in particular the sheath of the superior oblique muscle; being bilateral is an extremely rare event. We think that is important to bear in mind for physicians as a remote possibility in ruling out causes of headache.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
